From 805b8812e05e9c08aea4a68295b90591fab2cf87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:24:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] Serve Modern Warfare 2 (PS3)

MW2's older Demonware: batched lobby frames, bit-packed tasks and replies answered in order, publisher files
(playlists, MOTD) by id, the player's stats file (iw4-mpdata: listed, downloaded, created and updated, always the
signed-in player's own), matchmaking (replies echo the task id with one count; searches only get games of the same
playlist, playlist version and netcode) and the bandwidth test (service 18, message type 5), whose result decides
whether a host's lobby has public slots. Layouts from elliot1377/mw2-ps3-server (MIT) and Tustin/mw2-rpcs3's notes
on the game's parsers. Two copies matchmade and played Hardcore Free-for-all; stats survive a restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
